            <ArticleTitle>A review of the role of tricyclic medications in the treatment of fibromyalgia syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rationale behind the use of tricyclic medications in the treatment of fibromyalgia is reviewed. Controlled therapeutic trials have demonstrated significant improvement with these agents. However, important and sustained clinical improvement occurs in the minority of patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
